findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'The reviewer flagged validate() silently replacing invalid values (config.rs:88-96)
    and silent error dropping (main.rs:39), but never identified the core issue: from_file_or_default
    swallowing ALL errors including parse/permission failures via unwrap_or_default().
    TEA tests don''t cover this distinction either.'
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA listed 'CWE-209: Error Display doesn't leak internal file paths'\
    \ as a security test. The reviewer also flagged NotFound storing full URL (error.rs:13)\
    \ and noted eprintln!(\"{e}\") in main.rs:15. However, the core issue \u2014 CliError\
    \ Display with Io(transparent) leaking OS details via stderr \u2014 was partially\
    \ caught but not fully addressed."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote tests for 'CWE-113: Header injection via newlines in tenant\
    \ ID and token' (cli_client.rs:253,267). Dev implemented HeaderValue::from_str()\
    \ which rejects CRLF (client.rs:52,58). Reviewer verified this. However, the deeper\
    \ issue \u2014 using raw String instead of Option<TenantId> from axiathon-core\
    \ \u2014 was NOT caught. The reviewer even noted axiathon-core is declared but\
    \ unused. Partially caught (injection prevented, but type-safety gap missed)."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: The code changes summary shows Cargo.toml was modified, and the reviewer
    noted axiathon-core as unused dependency, but nobody flagged that dependencies
    like clap_complete, comfy-table, csv, dirs, reqwest, toml use direct version strings
    instead of workspace = true.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged: 'config.rs uses #[serde(default)] without #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]\
    \ \u2014 Unknown fields in the TOML config file are silently ignored... a typo\
    \ like servr_url would be silently ignored.' Also noted the token-in-config test\
    \ is vacuous (LOW finding). This directly addresses the silent token field issue."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: The reviewer noted the unknown-fields test uses 'let _ = ClientConfig::from_toml(...)'
    without checking the result, but did not identify the specific vacuously-true
    assertion pattern (is_none() || true). TEA wrote config tests but the specific
    assert!(config.server().is_none() || ...) pattern was not flagged.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged at LOW: 'cli_config.rs:141-152 token-in-config test\
    \ is vacuous \u2014 The test loads config... then only asserts server_url(). It\
    \ never checks that there's no token() accessor.' Also noted 'let _ = ClientConfig::from_toml(...)'\
    \ has no assertions. This catches the zero-assertion test pattern, though it was\
    \ rated LOW rather than given proper severity."
